Package: macpro-fand
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.8), systemd
Suggests: t2fanrd, resize-amdgpu-bars
Description: Zone fan control and 1228 W power budget for the Mac Pro 7,1
 Runs the four fans of a Mac Pro 7,1 (2019) through the T2 applesmc driver as
 four independent zones (MPX bay 1, MPX bay 2, CPU, memory side), each fan
 held by its own governor at the temperatures where the whole machine draws
 the least power, with hysteresis. Any alarm sends every fan to full speed.
 .
 Also keeps the machine under the 1228 W DC envelope of its power supply by
 managing the power caps of the GPU dies (amdgpu) and the CPU's RAPL limits:
 the worst case of every limit together never exceeds the budget, and power
 moves to whichever consumer needs it, CPU first. Each GPU die's cap also
 follows its temperature, holding it at a working temperature that limits
 leakage. Replaces t2fanrd as the fan owner; a clean stop hands the fans back
 to t2fanrd.
